ustifications.shp\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\u2022\tSE_US_grid.shp\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\nDocumentation Files:\n\u2022\tNCCOS-US-Southeast-Prioritization_BrowseGraphic.PNG\n\u2022\tNCCOS-US-Southeast-Prioritization_DataDocumentation.PDF\n\u2022\tNCCOS-US-Southeast-Prioritization_ExecutiveSummary.PDF\nData File Format(s):\t\tShapefile .SHP (and ancillary files .CPG, .DBF, .PRJ, .SBN, .SBX, .SHX)\nData File Compression:\tno compression\nData File Resolution:\t\tn/a\nGIS Projection:\tProjected Coordinate System: NAD 1983 UTM Zone 17N (Transverse Mercator: WKID 26917), Geographic Coordinate System: NAD 1983 (WKID 4269)", "type": {"id": "notes", "title": {"de": "Anmerkungen", "en": "Notes"}}}], "contributors": [{"affiliations": [{"name": "US DOC; NOAA; NOS; National Centers for Coastal Ocean Science (NCCOS)"}], "person_or_org": {"family_name": "Christine Buckel (christine.addison@noaa.gov)", "name": "Christine Buckel (christine.addison@noaa.gov)", "type": "personal"}, "role": {"id": "researcher", "title": {"de": "WissenschaftlerIn", "en": "Researcher"}}}, {"affiliations": [{"name": "US DOC; NOAA; NOS; National Centers for Coastal Ocean Science (NCCOS)"}], "person_or_org": {"family_name": "J. Christopher Taylor (Chris.Taylor@noaa.gov)", "name": "J. Christopher Taylor (Chris.Taylor@noaa.gov)", "type": "personal"}, "role": {"id": "researcher", "title": {"de": "WissenschaftlerIn", "en": "Researcher"}}}, {"affiliations": [{"name": "US DOC; NOAA; NOS; National Centers for Coastal Ocean Science (NCCOS)"}], "person_or_org": {"family_name": "Maria Bollinger (maria.bollinger@noaa.gov)", "name": "Maria Bollinger (maria.bollinger@noaa.gov)", "type": "personal"}, "role": {"id": "researcher", "title": {"de": "WissenschaftlerIn", "en": "Researcher"}}}, {"affiliations": [{"name": "US DOC; NOAA; NOS; National Centers for Coastal Ocean Science (NCCOS)"}], "person_or_org": {"family_name": "Christine Buckel (christine.addison@noaa.gov)", "name": "Christine Buckel (christine.addison@noaa.gov)", "type": "personal"}, "role": {"id": "contactperson", "title": {"de": "Kontaktperson", "en": "Contact person"}}}, {"affiliations": [{"name": "US DOC; NOAA; NOS; National Centers for Coastal Ocean Science (NCCOS)"}], "person_or_org": {"family_name": "NCCOS Data Manager (nccos.data@noaa.gov)", "name": "NCCOS Data Manager (nccos.data@noaa.gov)", "type": "personal"}, "role": {"id": "datamanager", "title": {"de": "DatenmanagerIn", "en": "Data manager"}}}], "creators": [{"affiliations": [{"name": "US DOC; NOAA; NOS; National Centers for Coastal Ocean Science (NCCOS)"}], "person_or_org": {"family_name": "Buckel", "given_name": "Christine", "name": "Buckel, Christine", "type": "personal"}}, {"affiliations": [{"name": "US DOC; NOAA; NOS; National Centers for Coastal Ocean Science (NCCOS)"}], "person_or_org": {"family_name": "Taylor", "given_name": "J. Christopher", "name": "Taylor, J. Christopher", "type": "personal"}}, {"affiliations": [{"name": "US DOC; NOAA; NOS; National Centers for Coastal Ocean Science (NCCOS)"}], "person_or_org": {"family_name": "Bollinger", "given_name": "Maria", "name": "Bollinger, Maria", "type": "personal"}}], "description": "\u003cp\u003eSpatial information on the arrangement of geological features, habitats and living marine resources on the seabed are often the foundation for decision-making in ecosystem management and ocean planning. Collecting information on the seabed depths and geomorphology is an expensive operation requiring airborne platforms like satellites, planes or drones, or small vessels to large research ships. Coordinating these data needs and data collection efforts will better leverage collective resources and meet shared goals. To help enable this coordination, in 2020 the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration (NOAA) National Centers for Coastal Ocean Science (NCCOS) developed a spatial framework, process, and online application to identify common data collection priorities for seafloor mapping, sampling, and visual surveys along shore and offshore of the Southeast United States (North Carolina, South Carolina, and Georgia).\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eTwenty-five representatives from federal and state agencies, academic institutions, and non-governmental conservation groups, designated seafloor mapping priorities using an online prioritization tool. Participants allocated virtual coins across 5 km x 5 km grid cells to denote their organization\u0026rsquo;s regions of seafloor mapping needs. Grid cells with more coins were higher priorities than cells with fewer coins.\u0026nbsp; Participants also reported why these locations were important and what data types were needed.\u0026nbsp; Results were analyzed and mapped using statistical techniques to identify significant relationships between priorities, reasons for those priorities and data needs. These data are the summarized results from this project and can also be viewed in an online web map (\u003ca href=\"https://noaa.maps.arcgis.com/apps/webappviewer/index.html?id=04cdd2a68c4f427f893f2042f326dc80\"\u003ehttps://noaa.maps.arcgis.com/apps/webappviewer/index.html?id=04cdd2a68c4f427f893f2042f326dc80\u003c/a\u003e).\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eSeveral common areas of interest were identified in the spatially explicit analysis of the responses.\u0026nbsp; Nearshore surfzone along Georgia, South Carolina, and North Carolina were highlighted by several agencies and organizations interested in sediment and sand resources as well as potential for rocky reef habitats.\u0026nbsp; Inshore estuarine areas were highlighted by state agencies and conservation groups interested in monitoring change in managed areas like National Estuarine Reserves.\u0026nbsp; On the outer continental shelf, areas near Blake Plateau off South Carolina and the continental shelf break off North Carolina were identified by federal agencies and conservation organizations as areas of sensitive habitats or historically significantly shipwrecks and maritime resources.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe seafloor mapping prioritization approach described in the Buckel et al. (2021, \u003ca href=\"https://doi.org/10.25923/qh2c-hs73\"\u003ehttps://doi.org/10.25923/qh2c-hs73\u003c/a\u003e) report associated with these data provides recommendations to organizations charged with mapping the seabed for navigation and commerce as well as resource assessments and management.\u0026nbsp; Already, the priority areas identified in this exercise are being used by NOAA to focus planned seafloor mapping missions.\u0026nbsp; Furthermore, the outcomes from this regional exercise contribute into a National Mapping Prioritization under the lead of NOAA to coordinate mapping activities across the entire US EEZ.\u0026nbsp; Together, these quantitative seafloor mapping prioritization approaches will enable improved coordination and more efficient allocation of resources needed to conduct seafloor mapping providing data to support environmental stewardship, safe navigation and commerce.\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;Additional information is available in the data documentation associated with this archive, for a complete description of methods and results see Buckel et al. 2021.\u003c/p\u003e", "languages": [{"id": "eng", "title": {"en": "English"}}], "publication_date": "2021-04-10", "publisher": "Zenodo", "references": [{"reference": "Buckel, C.A., Taylor, J.C., Bollinger, M. 2021. Prioritizing Areas for Future Seafloor Mapping, Research, and Exploration for the Southeast U.S. Atlantic Coast.  NOAA Technical Memorandum, NOS NCCOS 289.  71pp.  https://doi.org/10.25923/qh2c-hs73"}], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.25923/qh2c-hs73", "relation_type": {"id": "cites", "title": {"de": "Zitiert", "en": "Cites"}}, "resource_type": {"id": "publication-report", "title": {"de": "Bericht", "en": "Report"}}, "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "https://coastalscience.noaa.gov/project/prioritizing-areas-for-future-seafloor-mapping-research-and-exploration-in-the-southeast-us-atlantic/", "relation_type": {"id": "issupplementedby", "title": {"de": "Wird erg\u00e4nzt durch", "en": "Is supplemented by"}}, "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "https://www.noaa.gov/regions/southeast-seafloor-mapping", "relation_type": {"id": "issupplementedby", "title": {"de": "Wird erg\u00e4nzt durch", "en": "Is supplemented by"}}, "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "https://www.seasketch.org/#projecthomepage/5272840f6ec5f42d210016e4", "relation_type": {"id": "issupplementedby", "title": {"de": "Wird erg\u00e4nzt durch", "en": "Is supplemented by"}}, "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "https://noaa.maps.arcgis.com/apps/webappviewer/index.html?id=04cdd2a68c4f427f893f2042f326dc80", "relation_type": {"id": "issupplementedby", "title": {"de": "Wird erg\u00e4nzt durch", "en": "Is supplemented by"}}, "resource_type": {"id": "software", "title": {"de": "Software", "en": "Software"}}, "scheme": "url"}], "resource_type": {"id": "dataset", "title": {"de": "Datensatz", "en": "Dataset"}}, "rights": [{"description": {"en": "CC0 waives copyright interest in a work you\u0027ve created and dedicates it to the world-wide public domain. Use CC0 to opt out of copyright entirely and ensure your work has the widest reach."}, "icon": "cc-cc0-icon", "id": "cc0-1.0", "props": {"scheme": "spdx", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode"}, "title": {"en": "Creative Commons Zero v1.0 Universal"}}], "subjects": [{"subject": "United States Department of Commerce (DOC)"}, {"subject": "US DOC; National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration (NOAA)"}, {"subject": "US DOC; NOAA; National Ocean Service (NOS)"}, {"subject": "US DOC; NOAA; NOS; National Centers for Coastal Ocean Science (NCCOS)"}, {"subject": "Atlantic Continental United States Coast"}, {"subject": "NCCOS Research Priority \u003e Marine Spatial Ecology"}, {"subject": "NCCOS Research Topic \u003e Ecological and Biogeographic Assessments"}, {"subject": "NCCOS Research Topic \u003e Habitat Mapping"}, {"subject": "NCCOS Research Location \u003e Region \u003e Atlantic Ocean"}, {"subject": "NCCOS Research Location \u003e U.S. States and Territories \u003e North Carolina"}, {"subject": "NCCOS Research Location \u003e U.S. States and Territories \u003e South Carolina"}, {"subject": "NCCOS Research Location \u003e U.S. States and Territories \u003e Georgia"}, {"subject": "NCCOS Research Data Type \u003e Geospatial"}, {"subject": "NCCOS Research Data Type \u003e Derived Data Product"}, {"subject": "Earth Science \u003e Biosphere \u003e Ecosystems \u003e Marine Ecosystems \u003e Benthic"}, {"subject": "Earth Science \u003e Biosphere \u003e Ecosystems \u003e Marine Ecosystems \u003e Coastal"}, {"subject": "Earth Science \u003e Human Dimensions \u003e Environmental Governance/Management \u003e Environmental Assessments"}, {"subject": "Continent \u003e North America \u003e United States Of America \u003e North Carolina"}, {"subject": "Continent \u003e North America \u003e United States Of America \u003e South Carolina"}, {"subject": "Continent \u003e North America \u003e United States Of America \u003e Georgia"}, {"subject": "Ocean \u003e Atlantic Ocean"}], "title": "NOAA NCCOS Assessment: Prioritizing Areas for Future Seafloor Mapping, Research, and Exploration on the Southeast U.S. Atlantic Coast (GA, SC, and NC) and Outer Continental Shelf from 2020-02-01 to 2020-05-01", "version": "1.0"}, "parent": {"access": {"owned_by": {"user": "82378"}, "settings": {"accept_conditions_text": null, "allow_guest_requests": false, "allow_user_requests": false, "secret_link_expiration": 0}}, "communities": {}, "id": "4678430", "pids": {"doi": {"client": "datacite", "identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.4678430", "provider": "datacite"}}}, "pids": {"doi": {"client": "datacite", "identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.4678431", "provider": "datacite"}, "oai": {"identifier": "oai:zenodo.org:4678431", "provider": "oai"}}, "revision_id": 8, "stats": {"all_versions": {"data_volume": 185549199.0, "downloads": 33, "unique_downloads": 33, "unique_views": 665, "views": 681}, "this_version": {"data_volume": 185549199.0, "downloads": 33, "unique_downloads": 33, "unique_views": 660, "views": 676}}, "status": "published", "swh": {}, "ui": {"access_status": {"description_l10n": "The record and files are publicly accessible.", "embargo_date_l10n": null, "icon": "unlock", "id": "open", "message_class": "", "title_l10n": "Open"}, "additional_descriptions": [{"description": "Total File Size:\t5.57 MB total, 8 files in 1 folder (unzipped), (5.36 MB zipped)\nData Files:\n\u2022\tSE_US_Prioritization_Subregions.shp\t\t\t\t\n\u2022\tSE_US_SummarizedPriorities.shp\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\u2022\tSE_US_Products.shp\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\u2022\tSE_US_Justifications.shp\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\u2022\tSE_US_grid.shp\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\nDocumentation Files:\n\u2022\tNCCOS-US-Southeast-Prioritization_BrowseGraphic.PNG\n\u2022\tNCCOS-US-Southeast-Prioritization_DataDocumentation.PDF\n\u2022\tNCCOS-US-Southeast-Prioritization_ExecutiveSummary.PDF\nData File Format(s):\t\tShapefile .SHP (and ancillary files .CPG, .DBF, .PRJ, .SBN, .SBX, .SHX)\nData File Compression:\tno compression\nData File Resolution:\t\tn/a\nGIS Projection:\tProjected Coordinate System: NAD 1983 UTM Zone 17N (Transverse Mercator: WKID 26917), Geographic Coordinate System: NAD 1983 (WKID 4269)", "type": {"id": "notes", "title_l10n": "Notes"}}], "contributors": {"affiliations": [[1, "US DOC; NOAA; NOS; National Centers for Coastal Ocean Science (NCCOS)", null]], "contributors": [{"affiliations": [[1, "US DOC; NOAA; NOS; National Centers for Coastal Ocean Science (NCCOS)"]], "person_or_org": {"family_name": "Christine Buckel (christine.addison@noaa.gov)", "name": "Christine Buckel (christine.addison@noaa.gov)", "type": "personal"}, "role": {"id": "researcher", "title": "Researcher"}}, {"affiliations": [[1, "US DOC; NOAA; NOS; National Centers for Coastal Ocean Science (NCCOS)"]], "person_or_org": {"family_name": "J. Christopher Taylor (Chris.Taylor@noaa.gov)", "name": "J. Christopher Taylor (Chris.Taylor@noaa.gov)", "type": "personal"}, "role": {"id": "researcher", "title": "Researcher"}}, {"affiliations": [[1, "US DOC; NOAA; NOS; National Centers for Coastal Ocean Science (NCCOS)"]], "person_or_org": {"family_name": "Maria Bollinger (maria.bollinger@noaa.gov)", "name": "Maria Bollinger (maria.bollinger@noaa.gov)", "type": "personal"}, "role": {"id": "researcher", "title": "Researcher"}}, {"affiliations": [[1, "US DOC; NOAA; NOS; National Centers for Coastal Ocean Science (NCCOS)"]], "person_or_org": {"family_name": "Christine Buckel (christine.addison@noaa.gov)", "name": "Christine Buckel (christine.addison@noaa.gov)", "type": "personal"}, "role": {"id": "contactperson", "title": "Contact person"}}, {"affiliations": [[1, "US DOC; NOAA; NOS; National Centers for Coastal Ocean Science (NCCOS)"]], "person_or_org": {"family_name": "NCCOS Data Manager (nccos.data@noaa.gov)", "name": "NCCOS Data Manager (nccos.data@noaa.gov)", "type": "personal"}, "role": {"id": "datamanager", "title": "Data manager"}}]}, "created_date_l10n_long": "April 10, 2021", "creators": {"affiliations": [[1, "US DOC; NOAA; NOS; National Centers for Coastal Ocean Science (NCCOS)", null]], "creators": [{"affiliations": [[1, "US DOC; NOAA; NOS; National Centers for Coastal Ocean Science (NCCOS)"]], "person_or_org": {"family_name": "Buckel", "given_name": "Christine", "name": "Buckel, Christine", "type": "personal"}}, {"affiliations": [[1, "US DOC; NOAA; NOS; National Centers for Coastal Ocean Science (NCCOS)"]], "person_or_org": {"family_name": "Taylor", "given_name": "J. Christopher", "name": "Taylor, J. Christopher", "type": "personal"}}, {"affiliations": [[1, "US DOC; NOAA; NOS; National Centers for Coastal Ocean Science (NCCOS)"]], "person_or_org": {"family_name": "Bollinger", "given_name": "Maria", "name": "Bollinger, Maria", "type": "personal"}}]}, "custom_fields": {}, "description_stripped": "Spatial information on the arrangement of geological features, habitats and living marine resources on the seabed are often the foundation for decision-making in ecosystem management and ocean planning. Collecting information on the seabed depths and geomorphology is an expensive operation requiring airborne platforms like satellites, planes or drones, or small vessels to large research ships. Coordinating these data needs and data collection efforts will better leverage collective resources and meet shared goals. To help enable this coordination, in 2020 the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration (NOAA) National Centers for Coastal Ocean Science (NCCOS) developed a spatial framework, process, and online application to identify common data collection priorities for seafloor mapping, sampling, and visual surveys along shore and offshore of the Southeast United States (North Carolina, South Carolina, and Georgia).\n\n\nTwenty-five representatives from federal and state agencies, academic institutions, and non-governmental conservation groups, designated seafloor mapping priorities using an online prioritization tool. Participants allocated virtual coins across 5 km x 5 km grid cells to denote their organization\u2019s regions of seafloor mapping needs. Grid cells with more coins were higher priorities than cells with fewer coins.\u00a0 Participants also reported why these locations were important and what data types were needed.\u00a0 Results were analyzed and mapped using statistical techniques to identify significant relationships between priorities, reasons for those priorities and data needs. These data are the summarized results from this project and can also be viewed in an online web map (https://noaa.maps.arcgis.com/apps/webappviewer/index.html?id=04cdd2a68c4f427f893f2042f326dc80).\n\n\nSeveral common areas of interest were identified in the spatially explicit analysis of the responses.\u00a0 Nearshore surfzone along Georgia, South Carolina, and North Carolina were highlighted by several agencies and organizations interested in sediment and sand resources as well as potential for rocky reef habitats.\u00a0 Inshore estuarine areas were highlighted by state agencies and conservation groups interested in monitoring change in managed areas like National Estuarine Reserves.\u00a0 On the outer continental shelf, areas near Blake Plateau off South Carolina and the continental shelf break off North Carolina were identified by federal agencies and conservation organizations as areas of sensitive habitats or historically significantly shipwrecks and maritime resources.\n\n\nThe seafloor mapping prioritization approach described in the Buckel et al. (2021, https://doi.org/10.25923/qh2c-hs73) report associated with these data provides recommendations to organizations charged with mapping the seabed for navigation and commerce as well as resource assessments and management.\u00a0 Already, the priority areas identified in this exercise are being used by NOAA to focus planned seafloor mapping missions.\u00a0 Furthermore, the outcomes from this regional exercise contribute into a National Mapping Prioritization under the lead of NOAA to coordinate mapping activities across the entire US EEZ.\u00a0 Together, these quantitative seafloor mapping prioritization approaches will enable improved coordination and more efficient allocation of resources needed to conduct seafloor mapping providing data to support environmental stewardship, safe navigation and commerce.\u00a0\u00a0Additional information is available in the data documentation associated with this archive, for a complete description of methods and results see Buckel et al. 2021.", "is_draft": false, "languages": [{"id": "eng", "title_l10n": "English"}], "publication_date_l10n_long": "April 10, 2021", "publication_date_l10n_medium": "Apr 10, 2021", "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.25923/qh2c-hs73", "relation_type": {"id": "cites", "title_l10n": "Cites"}, "resource_type": {"id": "publication-report", "title_l10n": "Report"}, "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "https://coastalscience.noaa.gov/project/prioritizing-areas-for-future-seafloor-mapping-research-and-exploration-in-the-southeast-us-atlantic/", "relation_type": {"id": "issupplementedby", "title_l10n": "Is supplemented by"}, "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "https://www.noaa.gov/regions/southeast-seafloor-mapping", "relation_type": {"id": "issupplementedby", "title_l10n": "Is supplemented by"}, "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "https://www.seasketch.org/#projecthomepage/5272840f6ec5f42d210016e4", "relation_type": {"id": "issupplementedby", "title_l10n": "Is supplemented by"}, "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "https://noaa.maps.arcgis.com/apps/webappviewer/index.html?id=04cdd2a68c4f427f893f2042f326dc80", "relation_type": {"id": "issupplementedby", "title_l10n": "Is supplemented by"}, "resource_type": {"id": "software", "title_l10n": "Software"}, "scheme": "url"}], "resource_type": {"id": "dataset", "title_l10n": "Dataset"}, "rights": [{"description_l10n": "CC0 waives copyright interest in a work you\u0027ve created and dedicates it to the world-wide public domain. Use CC0 to opt out of copyright entirely and ensure your work has the widest reach.", "icon": "cc-cc0-icon", "id": "cc0-1.0", "props": {"scheme": "spdx", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode"}, "title_l10n": "Creative Commons Zero v1.0 Universal"}], "updated_date_l10n_long": "October 26, 2023", "version": "1.0"}, "updated": "2023-10-26T15:20:48.438108+00:00", "versions": {"index": 1, "is_latest": true}}' data-preview='false'>
